Hetero focus answers:
1. **§1 dual mode sufficient?** Yes — EAW F/W in both modes, +A under cjk; utf8/unknown default western (conservative); euc-kr/shift-jis excluded from auto but manually overridable. Honest v1 scope (`v1.1 可加 DBCS-source bit`). Verified against current mode-less `isWide` (buffer.ts:367) which excludes U+2500 — root cause confirmed.
2. **§4 IP strategy honest / missing?** No major gap now — A/B/C/D/E/**E2**(PROXY protocol + IPv6 egress)/F covered; whitelist honest-boundary note added (token + per-user limit + audit); residential pool discouraged as default. Correctly states no client-side source-IP spoofing in telnet.
3. **W1–W4 shippable without T1?** Yes — W1–W4+I1 are width-ship + docs, explicitly decoupled from T1/T2 (§5: T1 depends on network, not W*; T2 seeds marked `draft:true`).
4. **Security / open-relay?** Probe is read-only low-freq banner-only; seeds ≠ allowlist (§2.3 L3, §6); allowlist is destination policy in abuse plan (§4.4); PROXY protocol gated to "需基建 + 站方支援". No open-relay path.
